# Local Data & Integrations

## Local persistence

Business data is **local-first**. Use these entry points:

| Layer | Use for |
|-------|---------|
| `OfflineLocalStore` | Customers, workout plans, entities in Drift |
| Feature `*Store` / `*Repository` classes | Feature-specific reads/writes |
| `SharedPreferences` | Settings, drafts, exercise pins |
| `UserDataBackupService` | JSON backup export/import |
| `CloudBackupRepository` | Optional Supabase Storage snapshots of the backup JSON (opt-in, not sync) |

Always scope reads/writes by authenticated Supabase `userId`.

```dart
final store = OfflineLocalStore.instance;
await store.ensureReady(userId);
// use store methods — never raw Supabase for business CRUD
```

## Cloud backup snapshots (allowed, opt-in)

`CloudBackupRepository` (`lib/core/backup/cloud_backup_repository.dart`) may upload/list/download/delete
the same JSON envelope as `UserDataBackupService` to the private `user-backups` Supabase Storage bucket,
scoped per user via RLS. This is a **manual snapshot**, not sync: no automatic upload, no merge, no
conflict resolution. See `docs/sync-strategy.md` ("Cloud snapshots != sync").

## Do not add

- GymBlog.API client or `GYMBLOG_API_URL` wiring
- Remote sync replay without an approved plan (see `.cursor/plans/local-first-ux-v1.plan.md`)
- Direct Supabase table CRUD for coach/client/workout data
- Automatic/background cloud backup uploads (cloud snapshots stay explicit, user-triggered)
- Third-party workout app integrations (e.g. Hevy) without an approved plan

## Agent deny-list (do not reintroduce without approved plan)

- `lib/core/network/gymblog_api_client.dart` or any GymBlog HTTP client
- `GYMBLOG_API_URL` in env, CI secrets, or bundled assets
- `SyncOrchestrator` remote replay wired in `main.dart` bootstrap
- `get_it` or a global DI container
- Remote write paths via `PendingOperations` expecting server ACK
- Supabase `.from('...')` CRUD for business entities
- `lib/features/integrations/hevy/` or a `dio`-based Hevy (or similar) client
